WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.382 --> 00:00:01.831
- And now we are in the period of time

00:00:01.831 --> 00:00:03.809
where a lot of people are throwing at you

00:00:03.809 --> 00:00:05.924
a lot of stones by saying

00:00:05.924 --> 00:00:07.381
that's not going to work.

00:00:07.381 --> 00:00:08.716
A little discipline,

00:00:08.716 --> 00:00:10.924
you do little things.

00:00:10.924 --> 00:00:13.309
With a lot of discipline,
you do a lot of things.

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:14.783
How you know you have a hit?

00:00:14.783 --> 00:00:16.692
Stuff the media writing about you

00:00:16.692 --> 00:00:19.591
is how much profit are
you making from this car?

00:00:19.591 --> 00:00:20.661
If you are sure from the beginning

00:00:20.661 --> 00:00:21.618
going to hit all your targets,

00:00:21.618 --> 00:00:23.118
that means your targets are conservative.

00:00:23.118 --> 00:00:27.499
Don't plan too much.
(audience laughing)

00:00:27.499 --> 00:00:28.332
Doesn't work.

00:00:28.332 --> 00:00:29.729
If you don't start mapping

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.818
and establishing milestone,

00:00:31.818 --> 00:00:33.694
you're never going to be getting there.

00:00:33.694 --> 00:00:35.910
You need to have your own strength,

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.194
you need to have your own beliefs,

00:00:37.194 --> 00:00:38.042
make your own analysis.

00:00:38.042 --> 00:00:40.822
From time to time, making quick decision

00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:43.458
is going to hurt the
execution of the decision.

00:00:43.458 --> 00:00:45.991
You can't lead people in the 21st Century

00:00:45.991 --> 00:00:49.305
if somehow you don't assume
the consequence of your acts.

00:00:49.305 --> 00:00:52.315
- He's a French-Lebanese-Brazilian
businessman.

00:00:52.315 --> 00:00:54.501
He's currently the chairman and CEO

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.163
of France bast Renault,

00:00:56.163 --> 00:00:57.990
and Japanese based Nissan.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.867
In 2003, Fortune named him one of the 10

00:01:00.867 --> 00:01:04.573
most powerful people in
business outside the U.S.

00:01:04.573 --> 00:01:06.703
He's Carlos Ghosn, and here's my take

00:01:06.703 --> 00:01:09.062
on his top 10 rules for success.

00:01:09.062 --> 00:01:12.148
(cosmic whoosh)

00:01:12.148 --> 00:01:13.594
- You have to have vision.

00:01:13.594 --> 00:01:15.694
This vision has to be
based on understanding

00:01:15.694 --> 00:01:18.754
about the dynamics of the market globally,

00:01:18.754 --> 00:01:20.974
and then you have to pursue this vision.

00:01:20.974 --> 00:01:22.277
No matter what, you
have to built motivation

00:01:22.277 --> 00:01:24.342
inside your company.

00:01:24.342 --> 00:01:25.175
This is easy,

00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:26.008
because you're saying okay,

00:01:26.008 --> 00:01:28.496
we want to be leader in
technology that is meaningful

00:01:28.496 --> 00:01:29.532
for the consumer,

00:01:29.532 --> 00:01:30.365
and all the Nissan people,

00:01:30.365 --> 00:01:32.591
all the Renault people are buying into it.

00:01:32.591 --> 00:01:34.517
Then we need to come to the consumer

00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:36.817
and tell him, you know, tell the consumer,

00:01:36.817 --> 00:01:38.954
that's a great product
which is affordable,

00:01:38.954 --> 00:01:41.459
and on top of this is
going to allow you to drive

00:01:41.459 --> 00:01:45.807
without the guilt of the
melting of the icebergs

00:01:45.807 --> 00:01:47.579
and the change of the seasons

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:49.727
and the temperature, et cetera,

00:01:49.727 --> 00:01:52.138
and I think it's going
to be very powerful.

00:01:52.138 --> 00:01:54.478
But again, before it starts,

00:01:54.478 --> 00:01:55.559
there's always a doubt.

00:01:55.559 --> 00:01:56.908
And now we are in the period of time

00:01:56.908 --> 00:01:58.785
where a lot of people are throwing at you

00:01:58.785 --> 00:02:00.988
a lot of stones by saying,

00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:03.017
"That's not going to work,"

00:02:03.017 --> 00:02:03.850
and then you have a lot of comments

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:05.474
from competitors saying, you know,

00:02:05.474 --> 00:02:06.307
"You're too much bullies,

00:02:06.307 --> 00:02:07.140
"it's just not going to work."

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.672
Well, obviously, what you
want competitors to say?

00:02:08.672 --> 00:02:10.764
He's in the right direction?

00:02:10.764 --> 00:02:11.634
(audience laughing)
I'm saying, "Okay."

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:12.621
he's in the right direction,

00:02:12.621 --> 00:02:13.461
and where is your car?

00:02:13.461 --> 00:02:14.505
Why I haven't noticed your car?

00:02:14.505 --> 00:02:16.132
So what's your situation?

00:02:16.132 --> 00:02:19.956
(audience laughing)

00:02:19.956 --> 00:02:23.254
- So, going on perhaps a decade of running

00:02:23.254 --> 00:02:25.620
simultaneously two global companies,

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:27.680
how do you get the stamina to keep going

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.363
and to stay fit personally,

00:02:29.363 --> 00:02:31.770
and mentally and physically?

00:02:31.770 --> 00:02:33.441
- Well, you know, somebody said,

00:02:33.441 --> 00:02:35.924
"With a little discipline,

00:02:35.924 --> 00:02:38.044
"you do little things,

00:02:38.044 --> 00:02:39.387
"with a lot of discipline,

00:02:39.387 --> 00:02:40.542
"you do a lot of things,

00:02:40.542 --> 00:02:41.375
"and you start to discipline,

00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:44.658
"there is nothing which you cannot do."

00:02:44.658 --> 00:02:45.795
There was a lot of discipline.

00:02:45.795 --> 00:02:48.162
I mean, obviously, because
you're going to move

00:02:48.162 --> 00:02:49.512
from one world to the other,

00:02:49.512 --> 00:02:50.574
from one culture to the other,

00:02:50.574 --> 00:02:52.742
from two completely different company,

00:02:52.742 --> 00:02:54.888
you have jet lags, organization.

00:02:54.888 --> 00:02:56.811
People are expecting
you when you come down

00:02:56.811 --> 00:02:59.972
from a plane after 14 hours flight

00:02:59.972 --> 00:03:01.754
to be fresh and ready for them (laughs).

00:03:01.754 --> 00:03:03.661
They are not expecting to
see you to come and say,

00:03:03.661 --> 00:03:05.139
"Oh my God, this jet lag,

00:03:05.139 --> 00:03:06.792
"he cannot answer a question."

00:03:06.792 --> 00:03:09.385
They want you to be on
the goal all the time.

00:03:09.385 --> 00:03:11.803
So this requires a lot of discipline.

00:03:11.803 --> 00:03:13.405
You have to organize yourself.

00:03:13.405 --> 00:03:14.955
If you know you're going to do this job

00:03:14.955 --> 00:03:15.956
and you accept the job,

00:03:15.956 --> 00:03:18.725
you have to organize
yourself in order to do it.

00:03:18.725 --> 00:03:20.693
It's tough, but there is a solution.

00:03:20.693 --> 00:03:22.443
There is a solution for it.

00:03:22.443 --> 00:03:24.089
But it requires a lot of choices,

00:03:24.089 --> 00:03:24.986
personal choices.

00:03:24.986 --> 00:03:27.267
There are a lot of things
you cannot do, you know?

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:28.791
There are a lot of things you can do,

00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:31.597
but you're going to do them
within a certain order,

00:03:31.597 --> 00:03:35.388
but particularly with a lot of discipline.

00:03:35.388 --> 00:03:38.636
Are you going to be able to
make products who are hits?

00:03:38.636 --> 00:03:40.106
Okay?
First question.

00:03:40.106 --> 00:03:40.939
After one, two years,

00:03:40.939 --> 00:03:42.942
we started to renew the product lineup.

00:03:42.942 --> 00:03:44.838
We had some hits, some of them are major.

00:03:44.838 --> 00:03:46.763
How you know you have a hit?

00:03:46.763 --> 00:03:48.417
Stuff the media writing about you

00:03:48.417 --> 00:03:51.639
is how much profit are
you making from this car?

00:03:51.639 --> 00:03:53.588
That's the way you know you have a hit.

00:03:53.588 --> 00:03:55.088
The 350Z is a hit.

00:03:56.368 --> 00:03:58.035
The Murano is a hit.

00:03:58.887 --> 00:04:00.346
These are some of the most profitable cars

00:04:00.346 --> 00:04:01.187
we have ever had.

00:04:01.187 --> 00:04:02.020
That's why.

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:03.100
I mean, it's not only the media saying

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.623
this is a great car and
people are buying it,

00:04:05.623 --> 00:04:07.851
because you can have a
great car, people buying it,

00:04:07.851 --> 00:04:09.613
and not make one nickel on it.

00:04:09.613 --> 00:04:12.502
It doesn't mean that it's a hit.

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:14.493
Where the real hit is

00:04:14.493 --> 00:04:16.640
the product has to be successful,

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.395
but at the same time you need to sell

00:04:18.395 --> 00:04:21.914
as much as you think the potential is,

00:04:21.914 --> 00:04:23.293
and make money out of it.

00:04:23.293 --> 00:04:26.145
That's the real demonstration of faith.

00:04:26.145 --> 00:04:28.871
- You had pretty ambitious sales targets.

00:04:28.871 --> 00:04:30.047
Are you going to be able to hit those?

00:04:30.047 --> 00:04:32.171
- You never know until
the last minute, you know?

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:35.124
The objective of when
you make a long-term plan

00:04:35.124 --> 00:04:36.420
is not to make sure from the beginning

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.336
that you're going to hit them,

00:04:37.336 --> 00:04:39.061
because if you are sure from the beginning

00:04:39.061 --> 00:04:40.062
going to hit all your targets,

00:04:40.062 --> 00:04:42.452
that means your targets are conservative.

00:04:42.452 --> 00:04:44.329
That's the only way you can be sure.

00:04:44.329 --> 00:04:46.710
So you want to maintain
a certain stretched

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.236
inside the company,

00:04:48.236 --> 00:04:50.904
and being innovative and creative,

00:04:50.904 --> 00:04:53.421
and finding new products and new solutions

00:04:53.421 --> 00:04:54.701
in order to hit the target.

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:56.182
So it's risky,

00:04:56.182 --> 00:04:58.963
but that's a price to pay for development.

00:04:58.963 --> 00:05:00.630
Don't plan too much.

00:05:03.368 --> 00:05:04.201
Doesn't work.

00:05:04.201 --> 00:05:05.720
For me it didn't work, frankly.

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:06.889
Don't plan too much your career,

00:05:06.889 --> 00:05:09.406
because what you're going
to be facing in life

00:05:09.406 --> 00:05:11.005
is probably more powerful and much bigger

00:05:11.005 --> 00:05:12.731
than you ever imagine.

00:05:12.731 --> 00:05:14.296
So if you're following your plan,

00:05:14.296 --> 00:05:16.787
you may miss a lot of
opportunity coming on the side,

00:05:16.787 --> 00:05:17.620
but you don't even look at them

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:19.402
but saying, "Oh, I need
to continue on my plan."

00:05:19.402 --> 00:05:21.480
Okay?
Even though on the side

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:23.516
you're going to have a
huge opportunity coming,

00:05:23.516 --> 00:05:24.349
you don't look at them.

00:05:24.349 --> 00:05:25.182
So don't plan too much,

00:05:25.182 --> 00:05:27.056
or be flexible on the planning.

00:05:27.056 --> 00:05:28.556
You're going to have a lot of ordinary--

00:05:28.556 --> 00:05:30.963
Particularly in the
period we're getting in,

00:05:30.963 --> 00:05:32.325
2010, 2020,

00:05:32.325 --> 00:05:35.057
I think there going to be a
lot of transformation coming,

00:05:35.057 --> 00:05:36.411
and there going to be
a lot of opportunity,

00:05:36.411 --> 00:05:37.732
so be flexible.

00:05:37.732 --> 00:05:38.918
- I think you famously said,

00:05:38.918 --> 00:05:40.989
"Strategy is 5% of the answer,

00:05:40.989 --> 00:05:42.839
"and execution is 95%."

00:05:42.839 --> 00:05:44.595
So, what does that mean?

00:05:44.595 --> 00:05:45.772
And how did you actually--

00:05:45.772 --> 00:05:46.794
What did you do differently?

00:05:46.794 --> 00:05:48.444
- Well, you know the 5%--

00:05:48.444 --> 00:05:49.880
Yeah, I said, yeah.

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:52.317
5% of the challenge is the strategy,

00:05:52.317 --> 00:05:54.385
95% is the execution.

00:05:54.385 --> 00:05:57.592
This, I said it as CEO of Nissan,

00:05:57.592 --> 00:05:59.324
I said it also as CEO of Renault,

00:05:59.324 --> 00:06:02.032
and I said it as Deputy CEO of Renault.

00:06:02.032 --> 00:06:02.962
When I said it the first time

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.816
it was mainly in France,

00:06:04.816 --> 00:06:08.983
and that was to the top
management of Renault in France,

00:06:09.977 --> 00:06:12.389
because there was a
tendency in the company

00:06:12.389 --> 00:06:14.192
to spend too much time on strategy,

00:06:14.192 --> 00:06:17.431
and leave the execution for other people.

00:06:17.431 --> 00:06:19.084
And this is where I said,

00:06:19.084 --> 00:06:20.978
"Strategy's fine, it's very important,

00:06:20.978 --> 00:06:23.189
"but it's only the 5%.

00:06:23.189 --> 00:06:25.845
"If you don't go to execution after this,

00:06:25.845 --> 00:06:27.386
"the delivery and the performance

00:06:27.386 --> 00:06:28.893
"of the company's going to be very weak."

00:06:28.893 --> 00:06:30.530
I really believed it.

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.287
Now, it doesn't mean
strategy's not important,

00:06:32.287 --> 00:06:34.377
but when you establish north,

00:06:34.377 --> 00:06:38.247
and you know exactly where
north is for the company,

00:06:38.247 --> 00:06:39.945
you've done something very important

00:06:39.945 --> 00:06:41.678
because you're giving the direction.

00:06:41.678 --> 00:06:43.645
But if you don't start moving north,

00:06:43.645 --> 00:06:45.387
if you don't start mapping

00:06:45.387 --> 00:06:47.155
and establishing milestone,

00:06:47.155 --> 00:06:49.628
you're never going to be getting there.

00:06:49.628 --> 00:06:50.958
You're never going to be getting there.

00:06:50.958 --> 00:06:54.250
The same, nobody likes
people who are different.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:55.702
Usually we like to go--

00:06:55.702 --> 00:06:59.222
And you can go out with males, engineers,

00:06:59.222 --> 00:07:01.120
from the same schools, same education,

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.510
speaking the same language.

00:07:02.510 --> 00:07:04.260
It's much more comfortable.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:06.402
The problem is when we are all alike,

00:07:06.402 --> 00:07:08.648
we don't learn anything.

00:07:08.648 --> 00:07:10.547
It's comfortable, but we don't learn.

00:07:10.547 --> 00:07:12.036
Now, when you go with somebody

00:07:12.036 --> 00:07:14.225
who's completely different
from you, different background,

00:07:14.225 --> 00:07:15.462
it's more difficult.

00:07:15.462 --> 00:07:17.189
But we're going to learn a lot of things.

00:07:17.189 --> 00:07:18.344
Maybe you can learn a language,

00:07:18.344 --> 00:07:20.533
a different way of looking
at things, et cetera.

00:07:20.533 --> 00:07:22.318
Diversity is a wealth.

00:07:22.318 --> 00:07:23.925
But diversity has to be managed,

00:07:23.925 --> 00:07:25.937
and managing a cross-culture

00:07:25.937 --> 00:07:27.304
is something which is going to be

00:07:27.304 --> 00:07:29.211
at the same time very hard,

00:07:29.211 --> 00:07:31.456
but can generate a lot of potential.

00:07:31.456 --> 00:07:33.706
Don't work for recognition.

00:07:35.721 --> 00:07:36.605
It's an illusion.

00:07:36.605 --> 00:07:37.762
As somebody was saying, you know,

00:07:37.762 --> 00:07:39.605
if you want recognition,
buy yourself a dog.

00:07:39.605 --> 00:07:42.605
(audience laughing)

00:07:43.905 --> 00:07:45.323
I mean, don't work for recognition.

00:07:45.323 --> 00:07:46.881
You're going to be disappointed.

00:07:46.881 --> 00:07:48.332
You're going to be disappointed.

00:07:48.332 --> 00:07:50.450
Work for yourself.

00:07:50.450 --> 00:07:51.729
Obviously work for--

00:07:51.729 --> 00:07:52.668
Not matter what are your objective,

00:07:52.668 --> 00:07:54.278
if you want to become wealthy,

00:07:54.278 --> 00:07:55.313
if you want to, you know...

00:07:55.313 --> 00:07:56.957
I mean, work for yourself.

00:07:56.957 --> 00:07:58.166
Work for yourself.

00:07:58.166 --> 00:08:00.041
And I'm not saying that you
need to be egocentric now,

00:08:00.041 --> 00:08:00.874
looking, no.

00:08:00.874 --> 00:08:05.853
But I think do not put too
much emphasis on the outside,

00:08:05.853 --> 00:08:07.304
what the outside is going to be bring you,

00:08:07.304 --> 00:08:09.664
because you're going to be disappointed.

00:08:09.664 --> 00:08:10.497
You're going to be disappointed.

00:08:10.497 --> 00:08:12.421
And I want to tell you
why it's very important

00:08:12.421 --> 00:08:13.921
to hold this line.

00:08:15.864 --> 00:08:19.077
Because when you'll have
to make hard decisions,

00:08:19.077 --> 00:08:22.778
and probably some of you
will have in the future,

00:08:22.778 --> 00:08:25.040
you're going to be alone.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:27.204
Do not think that this is a team.

00:08:27.204 --> 00:08:29.274
No, it's not true.

00:08:29.274 --> 00:08:30.918
At the end of the day,

00:08:30.918 --> 00:08:35.102
the guy is going to make the
intimate decision is one,

00:08:35.102 --> 00:08:37.879
and this guy's going to do it alone,

00:08:37.879 --> 00:08:40.335
and he's going to do it
based on his own value

00:08:40.335 --> 00:08:42.622
and his own beliefs and his own analysis,

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:44.434
transmitted by his team, whatever, every--

00:08:44.434 --> 00:08:45.451
But at the end of the day,

00:08:45.451 --> 00:08:48.272
he or she is doing the decision.

00:08:48.272 --> 00:08:49.953
And then when you carry the decision,

00:08:49.953 --> 00:08:53.088
you're going to be
bombarded no matter what.

00:08:53.088 --> 00:08:57.023
So, if you're looking for
an outside recognition,

00:08:57.023 --> 00:08:58.556
it's going to melt you down.

00:08:58.556 --> 00:08:59.460
You're going to say, "Oh my God,

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:01.026
"that means it's not
working, everybody..."

00:09:01.026 --> 00:09:01.859
No, no.

00:09:01.859 --> 00:09:04.298
You need to have your own strength,

00:09:04.298 --> 00:09:05.543
you need to have your own beliefs,

00:09:05.543 --> 00:09:06.936
make your own analysis,

00:09:06.936 --> 00:09:09.505
and carry the decision.

00:09:09.505 --> 00:09:11.482
One of the things I learned
particularly in Japan

00:09:11.482 --> 00:09:14.225
that from time to time
making quick decision

00:09:14.225 --> 00:09:17.673
is going to hurt the
execution of the decision.

00:09:17.673 --> 00:09:18.506
Because what do you want?

00:09:18.506 --> 00:09:19.339
When you make a decision,
what do you want?

00:09:19.339 --> 00:09:21.857
You want to transform reality.

00:09:21.857 --> 00:09:22.972
You don't want to make a decision

00:09:22.972 --> 00:09:24.451
for the sake of making a decision.

00:09:24.451 --> 00:09:25.284
You're making the decision because

00:09:25.284 --> 00:09:26.994
you want something to change.

00:09:26.994 --> 00:09:29.998
So, your goal is the thing changed.

00:09:29.998 --> 00:09:30.994
That's your goal.

00:09:30.994 --> 00:09:32.360
So, now, the question is

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:34.382
when should you make the decision

00:09:34.382 --> 00:09:37.288
in order to make sure that
this thing has changed

00:09:37.288 --> 00:09:40.091
in the fastest period of time?

00:09:40.091 --> 00:09:41.687
So from time to time you have to wait

00:09:41.687 --> 00:09:42.657
to make the decision,

00:09:42.657 --> 00:09:45.207
because you're preparing
people to execute.

00:09:45.207 --> 00:09:48.203
From time to time you need to
make the decision very early.

00:09:48.203 --> 00:09:49.999
From time to time a little bit late.

00:09:49.999 --> 00:09:52.082
But when I say decisiveness mean

00:09:52.082 --> 00:09:55.304
capacity to take the decision
at the appropriate time,

00:09:55.304 --> 00:09:56.255
because at the end of the day

00:09:56.255 --> 00:09:59.493
what you need is reality changes.

00:09:59.493 --> 00:10:00.764
That's your goal.

00:10:00.764 --> 00:10:03.224
How can you ask your people,

00:10:03.224 --> 00:10:04.884
whoever they are,

00:10:04.884 --> 00:10:05.945
to do efforts,

00:10:05.945 --> 00:10:07.167
to go the extra mile,

00:10:07.167 --> 00:10:10.750
if somehow you don't
commit to the results?

00:10:11.786 --> 00:10:13.408
It's impossible.

00:10:13.408 --> 00:10:16.910
If people don't see that you
are working as hard as they do,

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:17.947
if you have too much--

00:10:17.947 --> 00:10:19.268
You have been at the top level,

00:10:19.268 --> 00:10:20.802
at all the level of the
company you have too much--

00:10:20.802 --> 00:10:22.911
As much as risk as they do,

00:10:22.911 --> 00:10:25.382
they're not going to follow.

00:10:25.382 --> 00:10:26.215
They're not going to follow you.

00:10:26.215 --> 00:10:28.470
So commitment is a very important part

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:31.553
of the management's tie of the lines,

00:10:32.647 --> 00:10:33.583
because in a certain way,

00:10:33.583 --> 00:10:36.164
this is one way to
stretch your organization

00:10:36.164 --> 00:10:37.413
and stretch people

00:10:37.413 --> 00:10:40.001
by putting the challenge
very clearly on the table,

00:10:40.001 --> 00:10:41.584
and no but and ifs,

00:10:42.884 --> 00:10:46.242
and what you have to dedicate everything

00:10:46.242 --> 00:10:47.970
in order to make the plan a success.

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:49.351
You're not going to spend
your time explaining

00:10:49.351 --> 00:10:51.404
why it was not successful, okay?

00:10:51.404 --> 00:10:54.747
And that's a big difference
between the Renault plan,

00:10:54.747 --> 00:10:57.120
and all the other plan
which were announced

00:10:57.120 --> 00:10:59.739
for the two weeks before and after

00:10:59.739 --> 00:11:01.455
where there was no commitment.

00:11:01.455 --> 00:11:02.288
Okay?

00:11:02.288 --> 00:11:03.383
If I come and see you and I say,

00:11:03.383 --> 00:11:05.314
"By the way, I'm going to do my best.

00:11:05.314 --> 00:11:06.272
"I'm going to reduce costs,

00:11:06.272 --> 00:11:07.751
"and eliminate 6,000 jobs,

00:11:07.751 --> 00:11:09.140
"and shut down three plants,

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:10.921
"and we're going to shut
down this operation,

00:11:10.921 --> 00:11:13.019
"and we're going to stop
this and that and that,

00:11:13.019 --> 00:11:14.279
"and you know, if it doesn't work,

00:11:14.279 --> 00:11:16.128
"we'll come back next
year with another plan."

00:11:16.128 --> 00:11:17.856
(audience laughs)

00:11:17.856 --> 00:11:20.369
You know, if I am working in the company,

00:11:20.369 --> 00:11:23.149
I say, "Hey, first, my
job is going to (unclear)

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:23.998
"what's going to happen with you.

00:11:23.998 --> 00:11:25.464
"I'm worried."

00:11:25.464 --> 00:11:26.297
Yeah?

00:11:26.297 --> 00:11:27.687
So I'm not going to
give a hand to this guy,

00:11:27.687 --> 00:11:29.438
because I don't know on top of this

00:11:29.438 --> 00:11:30.359
what's going to happen.

00:11:30.359 --> 00:11:32.094
If it's not successful,

00:11:32.094 --> 00:11:33.677
he's not committed.

00:11:34.955 --> 00:11:38.063
So, this, from the other side, people say

00:11:38.063 --> 00:11:38.896
you taking commitment?

00:11:38.896 --> 00:11:40.603
You're not smart.

00:11:40.603 --> 00:11:42.617
Because if you don't
fulfill the commitment,

00:11:42.617 --> 00:11:44.149
it's a bad consequence for you.

00:11:44.149 --> 00:11:45.281
Yes, that's it.

00:11:45.281 --> 00:11:46.779
We are in the heart of the issue.

00:11:46.779 --> 00:11:50.491
(audience laughing)

00:11:50.491 --> 00:11:51.536
You're at the heart of the issue.

00:11:51.536 --> 00:11:54.502
We can't manage in the 21st Century.

00:11:54.502 --> 00:11:55.551
We can't.

00:11:55.551 --> 00:11:57.988
We can't lead people in the 21st Century

00:11:57.988 --> 00:12:01.618
if somehow you don't assume
the consequence of your acts.

00:12:01.618 --> 00:12:03.252
And the consequence of
your acts can not be

00:12:03.252 --> 00:12:04.463
only, "I made a mistake."
No.

00:12:04.463 --> 00:12:05.582
From time to time,

00:12:05.582 --> 00:12:07.357
it's you have a vision, you have a plan,

00:12:07.357 --> 00:12:09.405
you have obstructions, you have objective,

00:12:09.405 --> 00:12:12.128
you're asking people
to work day and night.

00:12:12.128 --> 00:12:16.048
For them, you have to
assume them personally.

00:12:16.048 --> 00:12:17.910
That's the management of the 21st Century.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:18.743
That's it.

00:12:18.743 --> 00:12:20.625
And I think the strength
of the Nissan plants

00:12:20.625 --> 00:12:21.501
and the Renault plant

00:12:21.501 --> 00:12:23.539
is the fact that as these two companies

00:12:23.539 --> 00:12:26.186
are the only one doing
this kind of things,

00:12:26.186 --> 00:12:28.241
in a certain way they're
going to have a plus

00:12:28.241 --> 00:12:29.074
in term of performance

00:12:29.074 --> 00:12:31.182
because people are going
to feel much more motivated

00:12:31.182 --> 00:12:34.021
and engaged whenever you
have this kind of commitment

00:12:34.021 --> 00:12:36.233
or results, due to the efforts

00:12:36.233 --> 00:12:38.386
they're going to be doing.

00:12:38.386 --> 00:12:41.268
(cosmic whoosh)

00:12:41.268 --> 00:12:42.163
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:12:42.163 --> 00:12:45.437
I made this video because
Eric Chico asked me to.

00:12:45.437 --> 00:12:46.578
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:12:46.578 --> 00:12:48.546
that you want me to profile next,

00:12:48.546 --> 00:12:49.965
leave it in the comments below,

00:12:49.965 --> 00:12:51.000
and I'll see what I can do.

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:53.472
I'd also love to know which
of Carlos' top 10 rules

00:12:53.472 --> 00:12:56.041
had the biggest impact on you and why.

00:12:56.041 --> 00:12:57.539
Which did you like the most?

00:12:57.539 --> 00:12:58.619
Leave it down in the comments

00:12:58.619 --> 00:13:00.656
and I will join in the discussion.

00:13:00.656 --> 00:13:02.502
Thank you so much for watching.

00:13:02.502 --> 00:13:03.895
Continue to believe,

00:13:03.895 --> 00:13:05.661
and I'll see you soon.

00:13:05.661 --> 00:13:08.328
(cosmic whoosh)

00:13:11.617 --> 00:13:15.124
- I've never seen such a
thing as a boring leader.

00:13:15.124 --> 00:13:15.957
Nothing.

00:13:15.957 --> 00:13:18.867
Leader is always somebody interesting.

00:13:18.867 --> 00:13:21.914
Somebody who can connect with you.

00:13:21.914 --> 00:13:23.412
Very important, very important.

00:13:23.412 --> 00:13:26.491
I mean, if I'm sitting with somebody

00:13:26.491 --> 00:13:30.255
and after 15 minutes I want
to go to the next meeting,

00:13:30.255 --> 00:13:32.487
I know it's not very good.

00:13:32.487 --> 00:13:34.076
So, ability to connect,

00:13:34.076 --> 00:13:38.638
ability to be interested
and being interesting

00:13:38.638 --> 00:13:41.253
is also a very important feature.

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:42.236
And you know that this is something

00:13:42.236 --> 00:13:44.660
that you don't learn in
school or university.

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:46.432
It is something that
you develop by yourself.

00:13:46.432 --> 00:13:48.989
Everybody has his own skills, et cetera.

00:13:48.989 --> 00:13:51.211
So I would say, being a listener,

00:13:51.211 --> 00:13:53.184
being able to connect with people

00:13:53.184 --> 00:13:56.805
are two absolutely basic
condition for leadership.

00:13:56.805 --> 00:13:58.567
For the rest, you know,

00:13:58.567 --> 00:14:01.412
efficiency, ability to communicate,

00:14:01.412 --> 00:14:03.136
openness, curiosity,

00:14:03.136 --> 00:14:04.531
intelligence, et cetera,

00:14:04.531 --> 00:14:05.364
ah, that's fine.

00:14:05.364 --> 00:14:09.016
And we've seen great
leader who are not smart.

00:14:09.016 --> 00:14:10.447
We probably know a lot of them.

00:14:10.447 --> 00:14:11.913
I mean, they're not smart.

00:14:11.913 --> 00:14:12.746
I mean, yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:14:12.746 --> 00:14:13.579
They're very common.

00:14:13.579 --> 00:14:14.412
(audience laughing)
No, but it's true.

00:14:14.412 --> 00:14:15.727
I mean, they're not smart.

00:14:15.727 --> 00:14:17.912
And we've seen a lot of
people extremely smart

00:14:17.912 --> 00:14:20.794
who never were able to take
any leadership position.

00:14:20.794 --> 00:14:22.598
So I don't think this is
something discriminating.

00:14:22.598 --> 00:14:25.270
I've never seen a leader who was boring.

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:26.343
Or at least at the beginning.

00:14:26.343 --> 00:14:27.284
They may be boring at the end,

00:14:27.284 --> 00:14:30.007
you know, after five or--

00:14:30.007 --> 00:14:30.840
Never.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.862
And somebody who don't listen or observe

00:14:33.862 --> 00:14:35.366
or try to see, okay,

00:14:35.366 --> 00:14:36.774
what's the situation (unclear)?

00:14:36.774 --> 00:14:39.333
I am not going to challenge

00:14:39.333 --> 00:14:42.390
what you're learning at the university,

00:14:42.390 --> 00:14:45.002
particularly telling you that, you know.

00:14:45.002 --> 00:14:48.066
But when you go and you are a foreigner

00:14:48.066 --> 00:14:49.708
going to Japan,

00:14:49.708 --> 00:14:52.617
you're going to Japan for
one reason and that's it.

00:14:52.617 --> 00:14:54.408
It's turning around the company.

00:14:54.408 --> 00:14:55.241
Period.

00:14:55.241 --> 00:14:56.702
That's what people are expecting from you.

00:14:56.702 --> 00:14:58.498
How much you work, what do you do,

00:14:58.498 --> 00:15:00.248
if you have problems,

00:15:03.254 --> 00:15:05.680
if you have remorse, empathy,

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:06.634
nobody cares.

00:15:06.634 --> 00:15:07.555
Fix it.

00:15:07.555 --> 00:15:08.388
That's it.

00:15:08.388 --> 00:15:09.221
That's the message.

00:15:09.221 --> 00:15:10.054
Fix it.

00:15:10.054 --> 00:15:10.887
You accept the job,

00:15:10.887 --> 00:15:12.542
you have to fix it.

00:15:12.542 --> 00:15:14.842
We had two main problems.

00:15:14.842 --> 00:15:15.939
One of the main problem of Nissan

00:15:15.939 --> 00:15:19.318
is that we had 20 billion
dollars of debt in 1999,

00:15:19.318 --> 00:15:21.423
and no Japanese bank,

00:15:21.423 --> 00:15:23.177
and you know how flexible
Japanese bank can be

00:15:23.177 --> 00:15:24.908
for a Japanese company.

00:15:24.908 --> 00:15:28.346
No Japanese bank wanted to
lend any money to Nissan.

00:15:28.346 --> 00:15:31.694
So, we were facing a cash crunch, okay?

00:15:31.694 --> 00:15:35.018
This is immediate death, okay?

00:15:35.018 --> 00:15:37.838
So we need to reestablish the trust on it

00:15:37.838 --> 00:15:38.830
and cut the debt.

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:41.244
Second, you need to come
back to profits for 10 years.

00:15:41.244 --> 00:15:44.554
Nissan had 1% average operating profit,

00:15:44.554 --> 00:15:48.721
while Honda and Toyota
were around 7% to 10%.

00:15:49.613 --> 00:15:52.461
We had about 1% return on invested capital

00:15:52.461 --> 00:15:55.159
where our main competitors
were at more than 10%.

00:15:55.159 --> 00:15:57.100
So there was something wrong
you need to reestablish.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:57.965
You reestablish,

00:15:57.965 --> 00:15:59.618
just put it right.

00:15:59.618 --> 00:16:00.835
So I knew from the beginning

00:16:00.835 --> 00:16:04.049
that what was expected
from me is fix it, fix it.

00:16:04.049 --> 00:16:07.578
So when you know you need to fix it,

00:16:07.578 --> 00:16:09.742
you can say, "Okay, I'm going to make

00:16:09.742 --> 00:16:12.417
"as many changes as
necessary to fix the problem.

00:16:12.417 --> 00:16:13.801
"Nothing more.

00:16:13.801 --> 00:16:14.634
"Nothing more."

00:16:14.634 --> 00:16:16.283
So, changing the habits,

00:16:16.283 --> 00:16:19.134
if there is no obvious
result, you shouldn't do.

00:16:19.134 --> 00:16:21.159
But when you know that fixing the company

00:16:21.159 --> 00:16:24.224
is going to force you
to change some habits,

00:16:24.224 --> 00:16:25.057
while you're going to--

00:16:25.057 --> 00:16:25.955
You need to say it,

00:16:25.955 --> 00:16:27.784
you need to explain why you're doing it,

00:16:27.784 --> 00:16:30.617
and particularly, you need
to commit to the results.

00:16:30.617 --> 00:16:32.261
Because people don't like change

00:16:32.261 --> 00:16:34.156
as long as there is no commitment

00:16:34.156 --> 00:16:36.013
to specific results behind the change.

00:16:36.013 --> 00:16:37.964
Now, if you commit to specific results,

00:16:37.964 --> 00:16:40.778
they may give you the
benefit of the doubt,

00:16:40.778 --> 00:16:43.035
and that's exactly what
happened in the case of Nissan.

00:16:43.035 --> 00:16:44.365
- There is in our careers.

00:16:44.365 --> 00:16:45.546
- Very important, mentors.

00:16:45.546 --> 00:16:47.710
Very important, particularly,

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:50.960
but what they teach you what not to do.

00:16:53.558 --> 00:16:56.815
I had many bosses in my career

00:16:56.815 --> 00:17:00.707
because I started, you know,
like a simple engineer,

00:17:00.707 --> 00:17:03.457
and I learned as much with the...

00:17:05.249 --> 00:17:08.566
From the managers or the leaders

00:17:08.566 --> 00:17:12.690
who were making a lot of
things which shocked me,

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:15.161
as from the people who were inspiring me.

00:17:15.161 --> 00:17:16.823
Both of them are very important.

00:17:16.823 --> 00:17:18.486
Why?
Because the guy,

00:17:18.486 --> 00:17:20.892
you know, who is your boss,

00:17:20.892 --> 00:17:22.749
and all of a sudden you say, well,

00:17:22.749 --> 00:17:24.895
you know, he doesn't communicate well,

00:17:24.895 --> 00:17:26.893
I'm not motivated, et cetera,

00:17:26.893 --> 00:17:28.166
you're learning.

00:17:28.166 --> 00:17:29.573
You're learning the basics,

00:17:29.573 --> 00:17:33.186
because you're going to
always think every time,

00:17:33.186 --> 00:17:34.820
when you're in a big leadership position.

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:38.740
I don't want to become like X, Y, or Z

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:39.947
who were my leaders.

00:17:39.947 --> 00:17:41.833
I want to make sure that I'm interesting,

00:17:41.833 --> 00:17:44.025
I'm sure I'm associating
people, et cetera.

00:17:44.025 --> 00:17:47.350
So, the mentors are positive and negative.

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:48.951
You have the people who
are going to teach you

00:17:48.951 --> 00:17:51.059
what are the mistakes not to do,

00:17:51.059 --> 00:17:53.344
and there are the people
who are going to inspire you

00:17:53.344 --> 00:17:56.130
by saying, "Wow, I would have
never thought about this,

00:17:56.130 --> 00:17:58.991
"and I think this is very,
very, very powerful."

00:17:58.991 --> 00:18:01.016
So, you learn from both,

00:18:01.016 --> 00:18:03.849
and that's why it's very important

00:18:05.530 --> 00:18:07.471
to listen and observe and--

00:18:07.471 --> 00:18:08.327
You know, some people say,

00:18:08.327 --> 00:18:09.441
"You know, I have the boring boss,

00:18:09.441 --> 00:18:10.872
"I'm not learning anything."

00:18:10.872 --> 00:18:11.705
I said, "No, wrong.

00:18:11.705 --> 00:18:12.538
"Wrong.

00:18:12.538 --> 00:18:13.371
"You have the boring boss?

00:18:13.371 --> 00:18:16.178
"It's an opportunity
to see why he's boring.

00:18:16.178 --> 00:18:17.061
"What are the things?"

00:18:17.061 --> 00:18:18.910
Yeah, you know, what are
the things that I will learn

00:18:18.910 --> 00:18:21.333
that I will never have to do in the future

00:18:21.333 --> 00:18:25.454
so I am not boring for the
people who are in my team?

00:18:25.454 --> 00:18:27.107
If you have a great
boss from the beginning,

00:18:27.107 --> 00:18:27.940
you think--

00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:29.033
You're going to think it's very easy,

00:18:29.033 --> 00:18:30.129
you know?
- Mm-hmm.

00:18:30.129 --> 00:18:31.275
- Because the guy's interesting,

00:18:31.275 --> 00:18:33.619
and the objectives are
being hit, et cetera.

00:18:33.619 --> 00:18:35.325
You're not going to learn as much as

00:18:35.325 --> 00:18:37.035
when you're going to be facing adversity

00:18:37.035 --> 00:18:39.100
from a boss who has a lot of imperfection.

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:43.586
Obviously if all your
bosses are of this type,

00:18:43.586 --> 00:18:45.659
it's bad also, because
you never know what,

00:18:45.659 --> 00:18:48.373
you know, what is true north.

00:18:48.373 --> 00:18:51.794
So having some of both is very important.

00:18:51.794 --> 00:18:55.200
I was blessed by the fact that I had both.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:56.837
And frankly I learned as much from one

00:18:56.837 --> 00:18:58.587
than from the others.

